==Finnish==
{{Finnish index|m|ä}}
{{wikipedia}}

===Etymology===
From {{term|lang=fi|mäntä||archaic: mixing utensil made of the top of a young pine}}; cognate of Estonian {{term|lang=fi|mänd}}; originally the word meant a young pine, and now relatively rare words {{term|lang=fi|petäjä}} and {{term|lang=fi|honka}} were used of the older trees.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|[ˈmænty]|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|män|ty|lang=fi}}

===Noun===
{{fi-noun}}

# [[pine]], especially the [[Scots pine]], ''[[Pinus sylvestris]]''.

